The IP path between pc1 (195.11.14.2) and the partner host pc2 (200.1.1.2) is healthy. End-to-end latency is consistently low: 0% loss and ~2 ms RTT on standard pings, and large MTU probes succeed up to the path MTU (1472-byte payload, 1500-byte frame) as expected; larger DF-sized packets (≥1501 bytes) are locally rejected, which is normal and not a PMTUD blackhole. Throughput testing in both directions sustains ~130 Mbps, with TCP retransmissions only when we intentionally saturate the link. BGP is correctly exchanging 195.11.14.0/24 and 200.1.1.0/24, and FIBs on router1 and router2 point across eth0 as expected. Interfaces on all nodes report link up, full duplex, no errors; tc shows default pfifo_fast and no persis
